	(text "Backup source: one CR123A lithium primary in a board-mounted holder (sheet 2), behind an LM66100 ideal diode. Nothing charges it.\nWhy a primary: no rechargeable 18650 is rated for a sun-parked car (storage +45 C at best); a CR123A is rated to +60/70 C, and its\nonly consumer is a power cut the tracker already alerts on, so a spent cell is an event, not silent ageing.\nRuntime: ~5 months idle, ~8 weeks reporting hourly, ~18 days at 15-minute reporting.\nFirmware: CONFIG_APP_BACKUP_SUPPLY makes the tracker treat 8.5-9.7 V with ignition off as backup power; without it the 11.8 V\npower-off and 12.0 V sleep-safety rules silence it. A cut also wakes a sleeping tracker: at boost start sheet 3 lifts IGN to ~12 V\nfor ~0.4 s, and the firmware reads the ~9 V rail and reports the cut instead of a key-on. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.765 70.485 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b8080a4b-9888-4ee6-97e0-c2c1c1d0b675")
	)
